  "description": "YAVZON crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C91 H152 O38 P7 Tm5,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tm4 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm1 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm3 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm2 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm5 (Tm) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.742-3.756 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.58-108.33°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tm5(μ3-OH)(dipp)7(CH3OH)7(H2O)2]·5CH3OH·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
